---
// Cascade probe — VARIANT D (MEASURE-3, D-02 claim 3).
//
// Import shape: the exact reverse of variant C. `theme-charcoal.css` comes
// from this frontmatter and the design system's `tokens.css` arrives from a
// HYDRATED ISLAND (`TokensCssIsland.tsx`).
//
// This is the island-flavoured counterpart of variant B, and the same reason
// applies: it is the ordering in which the design system's `:root.dark, .dark`
// block lands LAST, so a charcoal token missing from the (0,3,0) dark block
// loses the (0,2,0) tie on source order. Testing only C would test only the
// forgiving half of the island case.
//
// The `client:load` directive is load-bearing — see casc-c.astro.
//
// The order of the two import lines below is load-bearing for the same reason
// casc-c's is, and casc-c's header carries the measurement. Keep the component
// import first here too: that is what makes this page emit tokens before
// charcoal while casc-c emits charcoal before tokens, so the island half of
// the matrix covers both orders rather than one order twice.
//
// See casc-a.astro for the full note on why the matrix is constructed.

import TokensCssIsland from "../../components/TokensCssIsland.tsx";

import "../../styles/theme-charcoal.css";
---

<html lang="en" data-brand="charcoal">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>probe/casc-d — theme in .astro, tokens from an island</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		<h1>casc-d</h1>
		<p>theme-charcoal.css from frontmatter; tokens.css hoisted out of a hydrated island.</p>
		<TokensCssIsland client:load />
	</body>
</html>
